# 0.1.18, Grab moves: Throw them up high, hook them again up there, Slam them down, on an enemy that stands alone:
# Eudora's Blarg trooper (QUEST_SIM_GIVE=12 QUEST_SIM_HOLD=12 QUEST_SIM_NEAR=427 QUEST_SIM_NEAR_AT=6,0, --level 4; Y at
# 1150 skips its arrival movie; he is put before it at about frame 1990). grabslam.sim does the same on Novalis, where two
# critters stand a unit apart: from OpenRAC 91b67c67 with the eyes' own view test, the one thrown up can meet the other
# on its way ("let go: it met another", half a blow each) and the slam is then not shown. Here: "[vr-grab] thrown up high",
# "the hook out to it in the air", "caught in the air: it hangs on the line", the hand yanked down: "slammed down from the
# line", "slot N let go: slammed into the ground", "slammed: the wrench's whole blow to it, half to N near". With
# 'QUEST_VR_OPTIONS=grab_launch 0;grab_slam 0' the swing up is a plain throw.
